Monitoring
Monitoring Setup

To improve cluster observability and health monitoring, open-source Kubernetes monitoring tools were configured and evaluated.

Metrics Server

Metrics Server was deployed in the Amazon EKS cluster to provide resource usage metrics for Kubernetes components.

Purpose:

Monitor cluster health
Monitor node status
Monitor pod status
Enable resource utilization tracking
Kubernetes Native Monitoring

The following Kubernetes commands were used to monitor cluster and application health:

kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A
kubectl get deployments -A
kubectl get svc -A
Monitoring Results
Cluster Health

All EKS worker nodes were verified to be in a Ready state.

kubectl get nodes
Pod Health

All system and application pods were monitored to ensure they were running successfully.

kubectl get pods -A
Deployment Status

Application deployments were monitored and verified.

kubectl get deployments -A
Service Availability

Kubernetes services and load balancer endpoints were monitored.

kubectl get svc -A
Open-Source Monitoring Tools Used
Tool	Purpose
Metrics Server	Cluster resource monitoring
Kubernetes Dashboard	Cluster visualization and monitoring
